{"reference":"1 Chronicles 11","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":11,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"David Recognized as King","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter opens with all Israel gathering at Hebron to recognize David as king. It then recounts David’s capture of Jerusalem, which becomes the shared royal center. Together, these events frame David’s kingship as recognized by Israel and established in a new royal city.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 11:1-9"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_011_076064903d6355cd602c88fe"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}